ISO-10303-21;
/* Tfa256: Single PLANE face, TWO wires: FACE_OUTER_BOUND is a valid 10x10 square (0,0,0)-(10,0,0)-(10,10,0)-(0,10,0); FACE_BOUND is a 2-edge slit inside the square, reusing ONE EDGE_CURVE E=(3,3,0)-(7,3,0) twice via two ORIENTED_EDGEs both .T. (FORWARD) — the coincident-edge pattern; unlike the single-wire Tfa074 (whose face has ONLY this wire and never satisfies the nbWires>=2 gate the removal repair needs), this face's second, ordinary wire genuinely gives it 2 wires, so the repair's multi-wire precondition is live and reachable; both bounds ARE wired into one ADVANCED_FACE on a live OPEN_SHELL; never orphaned */
